Third-party licensing
=====================

The Apache Cordova template in CordovaComposeApp/www and Cordova-generated
sources are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The Gradle
Wrapper scripts and JAR are also licensed under Apache-2.0; their original
headers and the JAR's embedded META-INF/LICENSE are retained.

The full Apache-2.0 license is in native/third-party-licenses/Apache-2.0.txt.
Attribution notices are in NOTICE.

Resolved Android runtime dependencies, their versions, declared licenses,
artifact hashes and evidence URLs are recorded in native/third-party-licenses/runtime.json.
Kotlin's standard library also includes code under the Boost Software
License 1.0; its full text is in native/third-party-licenses/kotlin-boost-LICENSE.txt.
Additional upstream copyright and license documents are in native/third-party-licenses/.

These statements cover the identified third-party works. This file does not
assign a new license to independently authored workspace code. The sample
application's package.json license field describes its Cordova template;
it must not be used to infer the licensing of all files in this workspace.

Installed build tools and node_modules are not included in the source or
APK distribution. If redistributing them, preserve their own complete
licenses and notices and review that separate distribution.
